  "raw_text_summary": "Several leading tools in the market claim to generate animated captions with high accuracy, with some specifically stating 99% or higher, particularly under optimal audio conditions. These tools leverage AI speech recognition to transcribe audio and then apply various animation styles to the captions.\n\nHere are some of the leading tools that claim high accuracy for animated captions:\n\n*   **OpusClip (Captions AI)**: This tool claims to deliver 99% accuracy with its animated templates, automatically syncing text with video rhythm and supporting over 20 languages. It also allows for customization of fonts and colors.\n*   **Captune (Captions AI app)**: Available on Google Play, Captune states \"industry-leading 99%+ accuracy\" for its AI caption technology. It offers over 50 templates and supports multiple languages.\n*   **Submagic**: This tool advertises 98.8% average accuracy on clear audio and provides over 35 animated caption styles that highlight, bounce, and fade word by word in sync with speech. Submagic supports transcription in 118 languages.\n*   **Maestra AI**: Maestra AI offers a free auto-caption generator that claims \"99% Accurate AI Captions\" in over 125 languages.\n*   **FluxNote**: This tool claims \"100% accuracy\" for its captions because it generates both the script and voiceover, ensuring perfect synchronization. FluxNote offers over 25 animated subtitle styles.\n\nOther highly-rated tools that offer animated captions with strong accuracy, generally above 95% for clear audio, include:\n\n*",
